      "title": "Foam smothers, cools and seals the surface",
      "description": "Water drawn through the ratio controller picks up foam concentrate at a fixed percentage (e.g. 3 %); the foam chambers aspirate air to expand it and pour it gently down the tank wall. The blanket spreads across the burning liquid, separating fuel from air, cooling it and suppressing vapour. Design follows NFPA 11 application rates (e.g. ≈ 4.1 L/min·m² for hydrocarbons with fixed outlets, longer times for some fuels — verify edition); polar solvents need alcohol-resistant foam.",
